halogen: WARNING 36.2 GiB of host RAM is in use before this server starts. The server sizes itself from the machine's total and leaves a fixed reserve for the OS and the model's 47.7 GiB lookup table, which is read through the file cache; whatever is already using those 36.2 GiB comes out of that cache. Expect every prompt to read the table from disk, prefill to run several times slower than published, and pauses of a minute or more. Stop the other workloads, or run this server on a host of its own.
halogen: WARNING: that budget is close to or over what this host has free (the engine refuses the last pin under 16 GiB of MemAvailable).
  If startup ends in "checkpoint: refusing to pin" or "HIP ... out of memory", lower HALOGEN_MAX_TOK to 16384 (the working memory, about 4 GiB back on the default checkpoint and 1.6 on w4b, for about 9% of prefill speed)
  or HALOGEN_KV_POOL_POSITIONS (the pool, ~29.5 KiB a position); a 1,048,576-position pool fits only with HALOGEN_MAX_TOK=16384.
halogen: WARNING 2841 compaction stalls (1820 of them failed) while 'weights pinned'. A healthy host does almost none: every clean startup measured here cost between 0 and 45 in total.
  There may be plenty of free memory, but it is in the wrong shape: large allocations each stop to compact it, most of those attempts fail, and startup can take tens of minutes at 100% of one core with no disk activity and no output. This is a state of the host, not of the model, and it is usually a large process that exited moments ago.
  Stop the other workloads, then either wait or run, as root:
    echo 1 > /proc/sys/vm/compact_memory
  and check that 'awk "/Normal/{print $14}" /proc/buddyinfo' is in the thousands before starting again.
